If a patient cannot taper an opioid and continues a high-dosage-opioid then every clinician should closely monitor the patient and should mitigate an overdose-risk with the patient.
If a patient cannot taper an opioid and continues a high-risk-opioid-regimen then every clinician should closely monitor the patient and should mitigate an overdose-risk with the patient.
A high-risk-opioid-regimen-example is a concurrent-benzodiazepine-prescription-example.
An overdose-risk-mitigation-example includes an overdose-education-provision-example and includes a naloxone-provision-example.
